          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
          "jcr:created": "Tue Mar 15 2022 17:47:43 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p>Stryker is working with its long-standing partner, the Red Cross, to direct additional financial resources to the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC) and International Federation Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies (IFRC) to support their relief efforts in Ukraine and in surrounding countries.<br>\n</p>\n<p>“As the humanitarian needs continue to grow, we are committed to supporting organizations that are helping the people being impacted by these devastating attacks,” said Eileen Buckley, Stryker’s senior director of corporate responsibility. “Our mission and values will keep driving our commitment to the health of communities.”<br>\n</p>\n<p>In addition to <a href=\"/content/stryker/us/en/about/news/features/putting-people-first-how-stryker-supports-worldwide-disaster-relief-efforts.html\">our continued partnership with the Red Cross</a>, we are partnering with other industry societies and our trade associations to support relief efforts.</p>\n<p>As the invasion of Ukraine continues, we remain committed to ensuring the safety of our employees, partners, customers and the patients they serve.<br>\n</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Mar 15 2022 21:01:28 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    }
